        "buildJavaScript": "You are helping a beginner student learning arrays in JavaScript.\n\nWrite simple code that updates values in an existing array called favoritesArray using reassignment.\n\nUse syntax like:\nfavoritesArray[0] = \"new value\"\n\nDo not create a new array. Do not use methods like .push(). Do not use loops or advanced syntax.\n\nReturn only valid JavaScript code. No explanation, no extra text.\n\nExample:\n\nfavoritesArray[0] = \"sushi\";\nfavoritesArray[2] = \"noodles\";"
